# husk 33 %: rejudge only), SQ-OB-02 (client row), SQ-OB-03 (row-text fault, tag is hearthandharvest:farmers_hats).
pace 1

## SQ-VH-06 | Heap floor and ceiling flesh per surface inside the Heap biome only; bedrock at 0 and 127
> execute in minecraft:the_nether run locate biome biomesoplenty:visceral_heap
waitlog (is at \[|Could not find) 120
capture H is at \[(-?\d+), (~|-?\d+), (-?\d+)\]
> execute in minecraft:the_nether run forceload add {H1-48} {H3-48} {H1+48} {H3+48}
sleep 60
> execute in minecraft:the_nether if block {H1} 0 {H3} minecraft:bedrock
> execute in minecraft:the_nether if block {H1} 127 {H3} minecraft:bedrock
> zqh biomesoplenty:visceral_heap {H1-48} {H3-48} {H1+48} {H3+48} minecraft:the_nether
waitlog \[zqh\] done 180
> zqh minecraft:crimson_forest {H1-48} {H3-48} {H1+48} {H3+48} minecraft:the_nether 1 126 minecraft:crimson_nylium
sleep 10
> execute in minecraft:the_nether run forceload remove {H1-48} {H3-48} {H1+48} {H3+48}
count Test passed >= 2
reject \[zqh\] error
look locate at -10 108 -2 (same seed); both bedrock Test passed; Heap floor and ceiling lines: flesh the top id of both, flesh (plus porous_flesh) at least 80 % of the Heap surfaces, the rest named; "on bedrock" floor count noted with the band line (judge against the band line: where on the floor the flesh sits on bedrock); "0 columns" = Heap not on any surface in the box: widen the box or move the centre. The crimson_forest line is a control (nylium expected on floors; if 0 surfaces, ignore)

## SQ-OB-04 | fruit pies and a Rustic cheesecake take 3 fruit; filling cans unchanged (one narrow query per pie)
> zq rdetail creativedelight:baking/apple_pie
> zq rdetail creativedelight:baking/pumpkin_pie
> zq rdetail creativedelight:baking/sweet_berry_cheesecake
> zq rdetail creativedelight:baking/grape_pie
> zq rdetail creativedelight:baking/syrup_cheesecake
> zq rdetail canned_apple_pie_filling_pot
> zq rdetail canned_pumpkin_pie_filling_pot
> zq rdetail canned_sweet_berry_pie_filling_pot
expect baking/apple_pie \{\S+\} -> 1 apple_pie <- farmersdelight:pie_crust
expect baking/grape_pie \{\S+\} -> 1 grape_pie <- farmersdelight:pie_crust
expect baking/syrup_cheesecake \{\S+\} -> 1 syrup_cheesecake <- farmersdelight:pie_crust
look each pie and the cheesecake: crust + 3 of its fruit + 2 sweet (pumpkin_pie: 3 pumpkin slices, grape: 3 grapes, syrup cheesecake: 3 syrup); the _from_filling recipes are crust + can; the three canned_*_pie_filling_pot recipes keep 3 fruit + 2 sweet + empty can (unchanged)

